   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">As part of its capacity building engagement under the Indo-Pacific Economic Framework for Prosperity (IPEF), Australia funded two workshops in Thailand and Vietnam, aimed at promoting stronger and more sustainable foreign direct investment (FDI) policy frame-works. The workshops, delivered by the Organisation for Economic Cooperation and Development (OECD), were attended by over forty participants from the public and private sectors. OECD speakers and invited experts shared international best practices and approaches to developing FDI policies based on risk management, transparency and alignment with national interest and domestic social and environmental priorities. For Vietnam, this capacity building supported ongoing work towards alignment with international standards on investment, which include the OECD Declaration on International Investment and Multinational Enterprises. The implementation of sustainable FDI policies benefits our region as a whole, contributing to a more predictable and transparent investment climate that promotes resilient, inclusive and sustainable development and economic growth.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
